<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.3.3: Dividing Polynomials Using Synthetic Division</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01617</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.3.3: Dividing Polynomials Using Synthetic Division</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ff9c145f-d6eb-40d2-b0d9-db3d7c2413a5</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity </title>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>In this activity we’re going to use synthetic division to divide a polynomial by a binomial.</para>
            <title>Part 1: Use Long Division</title>
            <para>You are going to solve a division problem using long division.</para>
            <para>1. \((x^2-13x+42) \div (x-6)\)</para>
            <para>Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>\[\begin{array}{l}x - 6\mathop{\left){\vphantom{1{{x^2} - 13x + 42}}}\right.
    \!\!\!\!\overline{\,\,\,\vphantom 1{{{x^2} - 13x + 42}}}}
    \limits^{\displaystyle\,\,\, {x\,\, - 7}}\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - ({x^2} - 6x)} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\, - 7x + 42\\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\underline { - ( - 7x + 42)} \\\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,0\end{array}\]</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <title>Part 2: Use Synthetic Division</title>
            <para>You are now going to solve the same division problem using synthetic division.</para>
            <para>2. \((x^2-13x+42) \div (x-6)\)</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>\((x^2-13x+42) \div (x-6)\)</para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 1 - </emphasis>Write the dividend with decreasing powers of \(x\). Make sure there is no degree missing from the highest degree down to a degree of \(0\).</para>
            <para> \(x^2-13x+42\)</para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 2 - </emphasis>Write the coefficients of the terms as the first row of the synthetic division.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_06_06_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 3 -</emphasis> Write the divisor as \(x - c\) and place \(c\) in the synthetic division in the divisor box.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_06_06_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 4 -</emphasis> Bring down the first coefficient to the third row.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_06_06_03.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 5 - </emphasis>Multiply that coefficient by the divisor and place the result in the second row under the second coefficient.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_06_06_04.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 6 - </emphasis>Add the second column, putting the result in the third row.</para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 7 - </emphasis>Multiply that result by the divisor and place the result in the second row under the third coefficient.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_06_06_05.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 8 -</emphasis> Add the final column, putting the result in the third row.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_06_06_06.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para><emphasis>Step 9 -</emphasis> The division is complete. The numbers in the third row give us the result. The \(1\) \( −7\) in the third row are the coefficients of the quotient. The quotient is \(x - 7\). The \(0\) in the box in the third row is the remainder.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <note>
        <para>Work with a partner to find each quotient. Discuss any differences you have in determining the correct solution.</para>
      </note>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\(
        (4x^3+5x^2-5x+3) \div (x+2)\)</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(4x^2-3x+1\); remainder of 1</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para> \((2x^3-11x^2+16x-12) \div (x -4)\)</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(2x^2-3x+4\); remainder of 4</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\(
        (x^4-9x^2+2x+6) \div (x + 3)\)</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(x^3-3x^2+2\); remainder of 0</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>\((3x^4-11x^3+2x^2+10x+6) \div (x - 3)\)</para>
          <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(3x^3-2x^2-4x-2\); remainder of 0</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
